SUMMARY:Pensacola Archaeological Society Lecture: Early Spanish Florida
DESCRIPTION:The University of West Florida's president emerita gives an ov
 erview of the first 250 years of the Spanish colony of Florida\, from 151
 3 to 1763. The talk covers Spain's shifting strategies to hold the Atlant
 ic coast and protect the gold fleets sailing from Cuba to Spain. The lect
 ure meets downtown at the Florida Public Archaeology Network's Coordinati
 ng Center\, and no pre-registration is required.\nPrice: not published by
